// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`Quick demo > agent: false composes with a fixed script; the manifest says compose; it renders to ready 1`] = `
"You are making version 1 of video vid_0001 (attempt <attempt>): a Quick demo from a screen recording, with no authoring.
Run these steps exactly, from the repo root. Don't write or change any file yourself: the scripts make the whole video.

1. Run: npx tsx scripts/prepare-run.ts --job vid_0001 --attempt <attempt> --manifest <manifest>
   If it fails, stop and report the error.
2. Run: npx tsx scripts/recording.ts analyze --media <media>
3. Run: npx tsx scripts/recording.ts plan --media <media> --target 24 --aspect 16:9
4. Run: npx tsx scripts/recording.ts compose --plan .va-run/recording/<media>/plan.json --title "Add a site"
5. Run: npx tsx scripts/check-contract.ts, then \`npx hyperframes check\` in video/. If either reports an error, stop and end your answer with it.
6. Run: npx tsx scripts/render-job.ts --job vid_0001 --attempt <attempt> --callback https://video.example.com/api/internal/runs/<attempt>/done --token <token> --upload blobs
   If it fails, stop and report the error; never edit files to make it pass.
7. End your answer with the fenced \`\`\`json block render-job.ts prints.
   Once it has succeeded, never run render-job.ts again: if its json block is out of view, print it with cat .render/<attempt>/manifest.json.

Progress (optional, best effort): after each step run: npx tsx scripts/checkpoint.ts --attempt <attempt> --url https://video.example.com/api/internal/runs/<attempt>/checkpoint --token <token> --message "<the step, in a few words>". It never fails the run; don't retry it or wait for it.

Never print environment variables. Never commit, push or open a pull request."
`;
